==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sorely}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sārlīċ|pos=adjective}}, {{m|ang|sārlīċe|pos=adverb}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|sore|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|sôrʹlē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsɔɹli/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɔːli/}}
* {{a|rhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{enPR|sōrʹlē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈso(ː)ɹli/}}
* {{a|nonrhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsoəli/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)li}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[sore]] or [[desperate]] manner.
#* '''1980''', Stephen King, ''The Mist''
#*: He said he wanted it [the picture] for his study. I would not let him have it, and he went away '''sorely''' puzzled.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=October 29, 2011
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Chelsea 3 - 5 Arsenal
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15413593.stm
|page=
|passage=If Chelsea hoped this blow would have a detrimental effect on Arsenal, they were to be '''sorely''' mistaken as the Gunners surged forward after the restart.}}

====Usage notes====
Some verbs commonly collocating with sorely: [[miss]], [[lack]], [[need]]

Some adjectives commonly collocating with sorely: [[tempted]], [[missed]]

